  "context_pill": "Section 33AB & Rule 8: Tea Development Account",
  "example_summary": "G Ltd. claims Section 33AB deduction for tea business profits, manages subsequent fund withdrawals for assets, and navigates the tax implications of premature asset sales and mis-utilization.",
  "source_provision": "### Statutory Summary Matrix: Section 33AB & Rule 8\n\n| Statutory Provision / Rule | Core Condition / Threshold | Tax Treatment & Legal Consequence |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Section 33AB(1)** | Deposit in Tea Development Account on or before specified due date | Deduction allowed is lower of actual deposit or 40% of composite business profits. |\n| **Section 33AB(4)** | Utilization of withdrawn amount for non-permissible assets (e.g. office machinery) | Deemed as profits and gains of business for the previous year of withdrawal. |\n| **Section 33AB(6)** | Utilization of withdrawn amount for specified non-depreciable assets | No fresh deduction under Section 33AB since funds originate from already-deducted deposits. |\n| **Section 33AB(7)** | Failure to utilize withdrawn amount within the same financial year of withdrawal | Chargeable to tax as business income in the year of withdrawal. |\n| **Section 33AB(8)** | Sale of asset acquired out of deposit before expiry of 8 years | Cost of such asset is deemed as profits and gains of business in the year of sale. |\n| **Rule 8** | Composite business of growing and manufacturing tea in India | 40% taxable as business income; 60% treated as agricultural income exempt from tax. |\n\n> [!IMPORTANT]\n> Segregation Requirement: When any part of a withdrawal amount becomes taxable under Section 33AB, the income must be strictly segregated into 40% business income and 60% agricultural income pursuant to Rule 8 before setting off brought-forward business losses under Section 72.\n\n> [!WARNING]\n> Asset Sale Restriction: Selling an asset purchased from a Tea Development Account within 8 years from the end of the acquisition year triggers immediate business income taxability under Section 33AB(8).",
